 adding a funding-rate break-even threshold metric to an existing Java project's `assess-income phase-one` evaluation.\n\nLet me first explore the repository structure to understand the codebase. The working directory is `/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree`.\n\nI need to:\n1. Read the task contract and other artifacts (but they say content is omitted, so I should read them from the ledger if possible — wait, the ledger write policy says don't create/edit/delete files under .agent/, but reading should be fine).\n2. Explore the repo to find the `assess-income phase-one` evaluation, the existing income calculation, costs, etc.\n3. Produce a design result JSON.\n\nLet me start by exploring the repository structure.\n\nKey requirements from the user request:\n- Add an explainable metric: in the same90-day window, capital, hedged notional, and fixed known costs, what cumulative funding rate is needed for funding net income to break even with simple earn (简单赚币).\n- Threshold = (existing simple earn90-day income + same-caliber full known costs) / hedged short notional amount.\n- AC-2 sample:20,000 USDT capital, APR0.0365,90 days, full cost20 USDT, hedged notional10,000 USDT → comparison income180 USDT, threshold0.02 (2%). Cumulative rates0.019,0.020,0.021 → incremental -10,0,10 USDT.\n- Tests cover zero known cost, zero APR, negative funding rates, and non-divisible precision scenarios.\n- AC-3: Evidence insufficiency — only provide numeric value when existing evaluation allows same-caliber precise net income comparison. Cost missing, quote terms unconfirmed, no historical settlements, or strategy still open at end of period → value unavailable, explain via existing blockers/unknowns.\n- AC-4: Evaluation service produces typed result, CLI only consumes. Clear labeling \"90 天累计资金费率阈值\" and unavailability. Add a concise usage doc.\n- AC-5: Regression and delivery on fixed isolated baseline.\n\nScope: ~6 files: existing service, result record, CLI, two tests, one new doc.\n\nLet me explore the repo now.","signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_8810446e8e0e44dc8edba7f1","name":"Find `**/*.java`","raw_input":"{\"pattern\":\"**/*.java\"}","input":{"pattern":"**/*.java"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_d0e468efdbe747a69ebe5b20","name":"Find `*`","raw_input":"{\"pattern\":\"*\"}","input":{"pattern":"*"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"Thinking":{"text":"Let me read the core assessment service and domain files first.","signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_74a0754368154f7cbf104062","name":"Read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java","raw_input":"{\"file_path\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java\"}","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_fd1cf1e575e441e6ba764e8d","name":"Read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java","raw_input":"{\"file_path\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java\"}","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"Th