ave a good picture of the existing code. Let me check the docs directory to understand where documentation lives (AC-4 requires a concise usage note), and check the existing docs list. There's docs/07-Calculation-Method.md and docs/08-Phase-1-Design.md and docs/09-Phase-1-Test-Runbook.md. A new doc could be added, e.g., docs/15-Funding-Break-Even-Threshold.md. Let me check the docs README to see the index.\n\nAlso, I should check the CLAUDE.md for repo conventions and check what tests exist. Let me also check the domain: `Recommendation`, `EvidenceStatus`, `TerminalPolicy`, `OpeningCost`, `FundingRatePoint`.\n\nLet me also verify AC-2 numbers:- capital20,000, APR0.0365,90 days:20000 ×0.0365 ×90/365 =20000 ×0.0365 =730;730 ×90/365 =730 ×0.246575... =180. Exactly:90/365 =18/73.730 ×18/73 =10 ×18 =180. Yes,180 USDT.\n- threshold = (180 +20)/10000 =200/10000 =0.02.- At cumulative rate0.019: funding income =10000 ×0.019 =190; net =190 −20 =170; delta =170 −180 = −10. ✓- At0.020:200 −20 =180; delta =0. ✓- At0.021:210 −20 =190; delta =10. ✓Now, the existing service computes `simpleEarnIncome` and `knownCost` and only produces `netIncome`/`incremental` when no blockers and no unknowns. The new threshold metric: `breakEvenThreshold = (simpleEarnIncome + knownCost) / hedgedShortNotional`. It should only be available (present) under exactly the same conditions as the incremental calculation — i.e., blockers empty AND unknowns empty. Per AC-3: \"只在现有评估允许同口径精确净收入比较时提供数值。成本缺失、报价条款未确认、没有历史结算或期末保持策略开放时，数值不可用\". So the availability condition = the same condition under which `estimatedFundingOnlyNetIncome` is present. That is: termsConfirmed && !ordered.isEmpty() && terminalPolicy != KEEP_STRATEGY_OPEN && unknowns (costs) empty.\n\nNote: knownTotal() treats missing costs as zero in the sum, but `costs.complete()` / `unknowns()` detect missing. The existing code puts `request.costs().unknowns()` into unknowns list. So when costs are incomplete, unknowns is non-empty → threshold unavai